CAT = "ieqfaCompetence"; SEG = "MCC"
Q = [
("The Minimum Competency Code mainly applies to people who:",
 "Advise consumers on retail products", ["Audit regulated firms", "Set interest rates for the euro area", "Draft new financial services laws"],
 "The MCC sets minimum knowledge and competence for staff who give advice or information on, or arrange, retail financial products for consumers, and for certain specified functions."),
("Under the Minimum Competency Code, which is a category of retail financial product?",
 "Pensions", ["Current accounts", "Foreign exchange cash", "Safe deposit boxes"],
 "Appendix 1 lists the categories, including life assurance, pensions, savings and investments, personal and commercial general insurance, private medical insurance, mortgages and consumer credit."),
("Which of these is excluded from the MCC's consumer credit category?",
 "Credit cards", ["Hire-purchase agreements", "Personal term loans for a car", "Consumer-hire agreements"],
 "The consumer credit category excludes credit cards, overdraft facilities, overrunning, high cost credit and housing loans, which are covered elsewhere or not at all."),
("A qualified person whose recognised qualification has no CPD scheme of its own must complete, each year:",
 "15 hours", ["8 hours", "20 hours", "30 hours"],
 "Section 1.7 of the MCC requires 15 hours of continuing professional development each year from qualified and grandfathered persons."),
("How much of a person's yearly MCC CPD must relate to ethics?",
 "At least one hour", ["At least four hours", "At least half of it", "None is required"],
 "The MCC requires at least one hour of CPD each year on ethics, and at least one hour for each function the person performs within its scope."),
("A qualified person completes 21 hours of CPD this year. What happens to the six extra hours?",
 "They cannot be carried forward", ["They count towards next year's total", "They reduce the ethics hour", "They are paid back as a refund"],
 "Surplus CPD hours in one year may not be carried into the following year under the MCC."),
("A qualified person falls short of the CPD hours for one year, with no earlier shortfall. Under the MCC, the shortfall:",
 "Can be made up by the end of next year", ["Ends their recognised qualification at once", "Must be repaid within one week", "Is simply ignored by the employer"],
 "A shortfall may be made up by the end of the following year, on top of that year's own hours, provided the person has had no other shortfall in the past five years."),
("Under the MCC, the most CPD a person can count from a single day is:",
 "Eight hours", ["Four hours", "Six hours", "Twelve hours"],
 "The maximum CPD in any day is eight hours, and no more than four of those hours may be on any single topic."),
("Who must accredit the CPD hours a qualified person counts under the MCC?",
 "A recognised qualification provider", ["The person's own line manager", "The Central Bank in each and every case", "Any training company at all"],
 "CPD hours must be accredited by the provider of a recognised qualification or by one of the professional educational bodies that provide recognised qualifications with a CPD requirement."),
("A new entrant working towards a recognised qualification may stay in the MCC training process for at most:",
 "Four years in total", ["Six months in total", "One year in total", "Ten years in total from joining"],
 "The maximum period a new entrant may spend in the training process is four years, with a pro-rata adjustment for statutory leave, serious illness or a career break."),
("While working towards a qualification, an MCC new entrant must:",
 "Work under a qualified person's supervision", ["Advise only on products under a set euro value", "Work only in the firm's head office", "Pass every exam within six months"],
 "A new entrant acts under the immediate direction and supervision of a nominated qualified person, who checks and approves their documentation in writing."),
("An MCC new entrant must register for:",
 "The first available exam sitting", ["Any sitting within five years", "A sitting chosen by a client", "A sitting of their choice"],
 "The new entrant must register for the first sitting they could reasonably be expected to sit and, if they fail, each available sitting after that until qualified."),
("Which situation allows a pro-rata adjustment to a new entrant's four-year MCC timeframe?",
 "Statutory maternity leave", ["Working part time all year", "A period of unemployment", "Extra annual holidays"],
 "Statutory leave, long-term illness of two months or more and a career break qualify. Part-time work, unemployment, retirement and holidays do not."),
("Grandfathering under the MCC can never be relied on for:",
 "MiFID investment services", ["Personal general cover", "Life assurance protection", "Private medical insurance"],
 "Grandfathering is not available for MiFID services, debt management services, crypto-asset services or, after 21 March 2019, mortgage credit agreements."),
("A call centre agent who answers only from a fixed script must, under the MCC, refer a question outside the script to:",
 "A qualified person", ["The Central Bank", "The customer's solicitor", "The firm's auditors"],
 "A prescribed script function needs firm training, a script written by a qualified person and supervision, and anything outside the script goes to someone who meets the full Standards."),
("Which of these is a specified function under the MCC?",
 "Adjudicating on consumer complaints", ["Cleaning the firm's branch offices", "Maintaining the firm's IT servers", "Preparing the firm's payroll each month"],
 "Specified functions include assisting with or deciding insurance claims, debt management, managing advisers directly, adjudicating on complaints and designing retail products."),
("Under Part 3 of the MCC, the Central Bank's role in recognised qualifications is to:",
 "Set standards and recognise qualifications", ["Write and mark the exam papers for each body itself", "Teach the courses in its own college", "Pick each candidate's study modules"],
 "The Central Bank does not take part in course design or examinations. It sets the competencies and confirms whether a professional qualification meets them."),
("To be recognised under the MCC, a new qualification's underlying academic award must be at least:",
 "Level 7 on the NFQ", ["Level 5 on the NFQ", "Level 9 on the NFQ", "Leaving Certificate level"],
 "Part 3 requires recognised qualifications to sit at level 7 or higher on the National Framework of Qualifications and to include CPD with an ethics element."),
("Under the Minimum Competency Code, a person who advises on MiFID investment products needs a recognised qualification and at least:",
 "Six months' relevant experience", ["Two years in the job", "A law degree as well", "A second qualification abroad"],
 "In line with the ESMA guidelines on knowledge and competence, MiFID advice needs an appropriate qualification and at least six months' relevant experience on a full-time equivalent basis."),
("Before a person is appointed to a pre-approval controlled function (PCF), the firm needs:",
 "The Central Bank's approval", ["A reference from a customer", "The person's tax clearance only", "Approval from the shareholders' AGM"],
 "Section 23 of the Central Bank Reform Act 2010 bars a firm from appointing anyone to a PCF role, such as a director or head of a key function, unless the Central Bank has approved the appointment in writing. For the largest banks, some approvals go to the ECB."),
("The Fitness and Probity Standards require a person in a controlled function to be competent and capable, financially sound, and:",
 "Honest, ethical and of integrity", ["A shareholder of the firm", "Resident in Dublin for two years", "A member of a trade union or professional body"],
 "The Standards have three limbs: competence and capability; honesty, ethics and integrity; and financial soundness."),
("Under the Individual Accountability Framework, who certifies that staff in controlled functions meet the Fitness and Probity Standards?",
 "The regulated firm itself", ["Each member of staff alone", "The Financial Services Ombudsman", "The Department of Finance"],
 "Since the Certification Regulations, firms must proactively certify that individuals in CF and PCF roles meet the Fitness and Probity Standards."),
("Under the Consumer Protection Code 2025, an intermediary may call itself a \"broker\" to consumers only if:",
 "Its main services use a fair analysis of the market", ["It is tied to a single product producer", "Its advisers all hold a degree in finance", "It has been authorised for over five years"],
 "Regulation 56 bars an intermediary from using the term \"broker\" unless its principal regulated activities are provided on the basis of a fair analysis of the market. An intermediary tied to one producer must say so in its communications (regulation 58)."),
("Under the MCC, a firm designing a retail financial product must ensure that:",
 "A key designer meets the MCC standards", ["The product is approved by the CCPC", "The product pays commission to every broker", "Every designer holds a law degree"],
 "Part 2 requires at least one key person in the product design decision-making process to meet the minimum competency standards for that product."),
]
